    "wacc_rationale": "AUD flows discounted at an AUD-built rate: AU 10yr government ~4.4% (Sep-2026) + 5.5% ERP x beta 1.2 = 11.0% cost of equity; pre-tax cost of debt ~6.0% (4.2% after 30% tax) on senior secured facilities; weights ~83% equity / 17% debt at market -> 9.85%, rounded to 10%. No ad-hoc E&P premium: commodity, reserve-replacement and execution risk are charged ONCE, in the scenario flows and the 30% bear weight (section 7f). Same WACC in all three scenarios.",
    "lease_treatment": "A (leases as debt): lease liabilities 35.6 in net debt; lease principal (10.0) NOT deducted from flows; lease-asset renewal is immaterial and sits inside the all-in capex_pct.",
    "restoration_treatment": "In the flows, not the bridge. Restoration cash payments (124.7 FY26) sit inside OCF; the model charges them through the all-in capex_pct (development + exploration + abandonment, Beach's own capex-guidance definition). The 991.8 provision is therefore NOT deducted as debt-like in the bridge - doing both would double-charge. Cross-check: base-case 10yr all-in capex ~5.6bn vs ~4.5bn pure sustaining (<450/yr) leaves ~1.1bn for reserve replacement + the 992 provision.",
