      "narrative": "Waitsia delivers a full year at or near 250 TJ/d and FY27 production lands mid-guidance (~21 MMboe, +8% revenue on flat realised prices); Moomba optimisation and Western Flank drilling add a further +4% in FY28. From FY29 the 8-year 2P reserve life asserts itself: production and revenue decline 2-4%/yr as Otway, Taranaki and Western Flank deplete faster than exploration and 2C conversion replace them. Underlying EBITDA margin holds ~54-55% on the Waitsia mix then drifts to 52% as fixed costs spread over falling volumes. All-in capex (development + exploration + abandonment, Beach's own guidance basis) starts at $700m (top of FY27 guidance) and settles at 28-30% of revenue, ~$100-150m/yr above pure sustaining (<$450m) to fund reserve replacement and the $992m restoration provision. Terminal value is capped at 7x FY36 FCF, roughly the reserve-life-adjusted multiple a buyer would pay for a portfolio with 2P+2C of ~330 MMboe today, rather than a growing perpetuity."
